# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# REAL CUSTOMER DATA — NEVER UPLOAD TO VERCEL
#
# .gitignore keeps this data out of git. It does NOT keep it out of Vercel:
# `vercel deploy` uploads the WORKING TREE, not the git tree, so every file
# .gitignore hides from a commit still went up with the deployment — and
# src/app/api/status/route.js reads src/data/status_data.json off disk at
# runtime and serves it. That is 365,440 RBL account numbers on a public URL.
#
# `npm run check:pii` cannot see this: it greps what git would stage.
# This file is the same guard for the deploy path. Keep the two in step.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The local data store: source CSV, canonical rows, explorer rows, batch payloads.
# Trailing /* then a negation — a file inside an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY cannot be
# re-admitted, so exclude the contents and re-admit the one safe file.
src/data/*
# ...except the model's measured credentials. Aggregate statistics only — no
# account, no name, no rupee figure tied to a person. The app imports it at
# build time, so if this is missing the Vercel build FAILS.
!src/data/validation.json

# Raw exports and anything derived from them.
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.tsv

# Eval artefacts built from the real book.
evals/reports/
evals/upload/
evals/sweep/

# Early HTML prototypes with real cardholder rows baked into the markup.
dashboard_preview.html
.preview_body.html
*_preview.html

# Secrets and local state.
.env*
.tunnel-url
